From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WavJaby <WavJaby@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:53:36 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] opengl: let the build choose USE_SLOW_BINDING

hooks.h hard-defines USE_SLOW_BINDING 0. Guard it with #ifndef so a
build can select the generic GL dispatch (CALL_GL_API through
getGlThreadSpecific) instead of the per-arch trampolines.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Patch-Reason: on glibc the thread pointer is glibc's TCB, so the trampolines' inline-asm read of TP + TLS_SLOT_OPENGL_API hits a glibc field; the generic path reads the slot through __get_tls(), which atl-bionic supplies as a per-thread array on every arch. A loader or environment cannot change a hard #define.
---
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
 opengl/libs/hooks.h | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/opengl/libs/hooks.h b/opengl/libs/hooks.h
index 86fec21bae5e94f10950cfd8842ca1103c2bd37a..5165042f652b311da1c95612edabbb8617f14921 100644
--- a/opengl/libs/hooks.h
+++ b/opengl/libs/hooks.h
@@ -34,7 +34,9 @@
 #include <GLES3/gl32.h>
 
 // set to 1 for debugging
+#ifndef USE_SLOW_BINDING
 #define USE_SLOW_BINDING    0
+#endif
 
 #undef NELEM
 #define NELEM(x)            (sizeof(x)/sizeof(*(x)))
